local_patch_display_failure=patches/x11-display-failure.patch checks failed XOpenDisplay before display use and retires partial X11 initialization; repeated failure and subsequent window creation are regression tested
local_patch=RGFW_NO_XINPUT2 guard; unused optional XRandR/XInput2 compile closure disabled by lib/presentation; bounded X11 custom clipboard target hook for native bitmap copy; macOS blits use an owned RGBA bitmap and preserve caller pixels (patches/macos-owned-bitmap.patch); macOS reuses process-lifetime Objective-C classes across RGFW reinitialization (patches/macos-reuse-classes.patch); Linux X11 extension unload clears cached Xcursor/Xi/Xext callables so subsequent initialization rebinds them (patches/x11-library-lifetime.patch); no crash-causality claim
local_patch_x11_clipboard=patches/x11-clipboard-length.patch sends UTF8_STRING and MULTIPLE text without the internal NUL terminator
local_patch_x11_atoms=patches/x11-atom-display-lifetime.patch interns X11 atoms on the current display so reinitialization after server reset never reuses stale IDs
local_patch_x11_key_modifiers=patches/x11-key-modifiers.patch snapshots modifiers into queued X11 key press and release events so clipboard and navigation handlers observe the state at event time
local_patch_macos_event_wait=patches/macos-event-wait.patch converts finite event waits from milliseconds to seconds and maps negative waits to distantFuture
